    "about": {
      "t01": "Our story",
      "t02": "MIM is an Egyptian label that hand prints every piece with real leaves, sunlight and carved wooden blocks, so each one is as unique as the person who wears it.",
      "t03": "Read the story",
      "t04": "We return to our roots and revive ancient hand printing techniques. We celebrate the diversity and individuality of every customer. A piece of our soul is in everything we make, and no two pieces are ever the same.",
      "t05": "May Esayed · Founder & designer",
      "t06": "About the designer",
      "t07": "A love of leaves that started in childhood",
      "t08": "Our techniques",
      "t09": "Five ways we print nature onto fabric",
      "t10": "Shop this print",
      "t11": "From the collection",
      "t12": "Our team",
      "t13": "The hands behind every piece",
      "t14": "Our dedicated team is behind every single step of production, putting passion and care into making every MIM piece stand out.",
      "t15": "Find your one-of-a-kind piece",
      "t16": "Shop new in",
      "t17": "Contact us",
      "t18": "Egyptian roots|Printed by hand|One of a kind|Made for every woman",
      "t19": "The symbols and rich history of ancient Egypt are our first source of inspiration.|Real leaves, carved wooden blocks and Egyptian sun. No machine prints.|Every leaf leaves its own mark, so no two pieces are ever alike.|Easy shapes and free sizes that celebrate every body and every style.",
      "t20": "Leaf printing|Eco printing|Block printing|Sun printing|Textile art",
      "t21": "Every leaf has its own character and story, leaving a beautiful individual print that makes each piece as unique as its wearer.|Leaves, flowers and bark are rolled tightly into the fabric and steamed, so their natural pigments and shapes transfer onto it. Each print is shaped by the plant, the season and the water.|Carved wooden and linoleum blocks with motifs drawn from our rich heritage give our pieces a timeless, vintage feel.|A photographic process first discovered in 1842. The fabric is prepared in a darkroom, then laid out under the sun with real leaves, revealing each one in deep Prussian blue.|Fabric is sprayed with dye through stencils and ornaments inspired by our culture, building rhythm, symmetry and layers that turn each dress into a piece of textile art.",
      "t22": "The MIM studio",
      "t23": "Cutting, printing & finishing",
      "h1a": "Nature.",
      "h1b": "History.",
      "h1c": "Fashion.",
      "f1": "May has a lasting fascination with nature and energy. Her passion began as a child and grew during a visit to Germany, where she took long walks in the forest and collected every new leaf shape she found. Her host family gave her a botanical encyclopedia, and her first herbarium was born.",
      "f2": "She later worked as a tour guide for years, finding peace among Egypt's historical sites and a deep connection with its ancient symbols. Bringing her love of nature and history together, she began using ancient hand printing techniques to print natural leaf patterns on her pieces.",
      "quote": "\"Pieces that bring joy and balance into people's lives.\"",
      "f3": "With her studies in holistic healing and colour therapy, every collection is an expression of everything she has learned, and continues to learn, every day.",
      "n1": "May Esayed",
      "r1": "Founder & designer",
      "n2": "Eman Hussein",
      "r2": "Visual artist & head printmaker",
      "n3": "The MIM studio",
      "r3": "Cutting, printing & finishing"
    },
